   "Northwind-negotiator": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting of all confirmed incidents within 24 hours and customer notice within 48 hours, but scope is limited to confirmed incidents (acceptable). S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% limit but does not stop sales above the limit and keeps per-model results from customers and the public (weakened). S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 24 months and allows a 6-year retrofit with feasibility escape (weakened). S4 requires built-in suppression by 36 months (acceptable). S5 makes recall discretionary despite an 8/100k notification trigger and requires customer notices with test results within 48 hours (weakened)."
